# /etc/sudoers.d/11-engine-files: installed by build-engine (installUdev -> installEngineSudoers),
# mode 0440, owner root:root. Validate with: visudo -cf <file>
#
# Files and folders the Engine (running as pi under pm2) writes or removes as root
# under /disks (idea#121, idea#126). 10-engine lists the Engine's other root
# commands and is not changed by this file.
# Keep this file in sync with the code:
#   META.yaml    src/data/Meta.ts (writeMetaFile, runSudoTee: first dock of a disk
#                without META.yaml; the mount roots under /disks are root:root)
#   mount point  src/monitors/mounts.ts (removeMountPointFolder: undock and startup
#                cleanup remove /disks/<device> after `mountpoint -q` says it is no
#                longer a mount point; never rm -fr)
#
# The code runs `sudo /usr/bin/tee /disks/<device>/META.yaml > /dev/null` with the
# YAML on stdin, so sudo sees exactly "/usr/bin/tee /disks/<device>/META.yaml", and
# `sudo /usr/bin/rmdir /disks/<device>`, so sudo sees exactly that. rmdir only
# removes an empty folder, so it can never delete a disk's data.
# Patterns are narrow on purpose (sd[a-z][12], never /disks/*): in sudoers a '*' in
# arguments also matches spaces, '/' and '..'. tee without -a truncates the file.
# Paths are for Raspberry Pi OS (merged /usr).
pi ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tee /disks/sd[a-z][12]/META.yaml
pi ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/rmdir /disks/sd[a-z][12]
